@stmol/dsh-rub-cost README · What the card shows：Every ruble amount is shown with two decimals. The price list also keeps two and
adds a third or fourth digit when needed to preserve a finer rate. The token breakdown stays out of the
card, because the neighbouring "Token usage" cell already prints it.

@stmol/dsh-rub-cost README · Editing prices and the rate：`MODEL_PRICES`, `BILLING_CURRENCY` and `RATE_URL` sit at the top of `client.js`;
`DEFAULT_OFFSET_MS` next to them is the fallback clock offset (UTC+3) for a
browser that reports none. After an edit the bundle has to be reinstalled: remove
and add the plugin in the UI, or `dsh plugin add <path-to-plugin-directory>`.
